    {
      "source": "Doctors of Running",
      "priority": 3,
      "url": "https://www.doctorsofrunning.com/2025/12/mizuno-hyperwarp-elite-review-2026.html",
      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "Cushioning: The dual-density PEBA + supercritical TPE midsole and 38/34.5 mm stack provide plenty of cushioning with a predictable ride; the heel bevel is gradual and the forefoot feels best when loaded hard.",
        "Responsiveness: It delivers a strong weight-to-responsiveness ratio, with a stiff plate and clear pop on forceful toe-offs; snappiness fades when fatigue shifts loading backward because the rocker is gentler/later.",
        "Stability: A wide platform (especially in the forefoot), carbon-plated torsional stiffness, secure lockdown, and confident cornering make it very sure-footed; even without a formal heel counter, heel hold was reported as stable.",
        "Durability: Outsole traction is good (mostly forefoot), the upper mesh is described as sturdy and holding up well under load, and the review’s durability expectation is rated good with no early wear issues noted."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "Road Trail Run",
      "priority": 4,
      "url": "https://www.roadtrailrun.com/2025/12/mizuno-hyperwarp-elite-review-5.html",
      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "Cushioning: The ride is firmer and harsher than expected for a 38 mm heel stack, feels lower/minimal underfoot, and offers less long-distance impact protection than the specs suggest.",
        "Responsiveness: The PEBA top layer and full-length carbon plate produce strong snap, quick forefoot engagement, and fast turnover, making it feel very nimble and race-aggressive.",
        "Stability: The firmer TPEE base and rigid plated structure provide solid mechanical stability for its weight, but the narrow platform and minimal heel counter make it less supportive for heel-strikers or runners needing more lateral/heel support.",
        "Durability: The firmer TPEE base is positioned for better longevity, and the thin G3 outsole showed acceptable grip in limited use, but long-term outsole wear remains unproven from this review."
      ]
    }
  ],
